// =============================================================================
//  dttxorg-patch.xcconfig
//  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Compile-time flags for the "no-license-wall, no-auto-update" personal build.
//
//  Apply this file (or copy the values out) once per fresh checkout:
//
//      Xcode → File → Project Settings... (or Workspace Settings...) →
//      Based on Configuration File → *select this xcconfig* for every
//      Mac Mouse Fix build configuration you plan to use (Debug / Release).
//
//  Equivalently, you can paste the SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS and
//  GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS values into the project's Build Settings
//  directly — they're just three flags total.
//
//  Author of the patch: zhuli (dttxorg30@gmail.com)
//  Patch branch:       patch/disable-updates-and-license-wall
// =============================================================================


// --- Swift: kill the 30-day trial + Gumroad license check ------------------
// FORCE_LICENSED already exists in upstream code (see License.swift
// licenseStateFromOverrides()). Setting it makes the override branch return
// MFLicenseState(isLicensed: true, ...) for every run.
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) FORCE_LICENSED


// --- C / Objective-C / C++: kill Sparkle updater ---------------------------
// DISABLE_UPDATES is a NEW flag introduced in this patch. See the `#if
// DISABLE_UPDATES` block in App/AppDelegate.m — the entire updater
// initialization is compiled out, so no network request ever goes to the
// upstream appcast. The Info.plist SUFeedURL is also redirected to
// 127.0.0.1 as a second line of defense.
GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS = $(inherited) DISABLE_UPDATES=1
